body:
Fixes #10867
Clause-②: yes (narrowing). Published `@object-ui/types` members narrow: the separator arm of `NavigationItem` loses `label`, and `AppWizardDraft` loses `layout`. That makes this `minor` plus a BREAKING (authoring) banner, and never `major`.

Dispatched by the `domain:ui` seat 2 PM (claim comment 5861866471, triage 5861615446), session `https://claude.ai/code/session_014mXUNuFomfj24w7s1pZzhN` (`mode:subagent`, so that id is also this run's). Branch `claude/issue-10867-app-wizard-saves-spec-app`, cut from `origin/main` `b93e245f9` (BASE); head `2c19f3047` after fix round 1 (round-0 head `e2493c796`).

## What changed

**Member 1 — a separator carries only `type`, `id` and `order` (the p1).**
- `@object-ui/types`: `NavigationItem` is now a union of two arms, discriminated by `type`. `NavigationEntryItem` is the former interface with `type` narrowed to every spec nav type except `'separator'`, and it keeps its required `label`. `NavigationSeparatorItem` admits `type`, `id` and `order`, the spec separator's keys, and every other entry key is `?: never` on it. Those `never` keys are derived from `NavigationEntryItem`, so a key added there is refused on the separator without an edit. Both arms are exported from the package root. `menuItemToNavigationItem` maps a legacy separator to `{ id, type: 'separator' }` and drops its label.
- `spec-derived-unions.test.ts`: the blocker-3 pin (`_specSeparatorStillHasNoLabel`) is lifted. It is replaced by three agreement pins. `_separatorAdmitsTheSpecKeys` and `_separatorAdmitsTheSpecInputKeys` say the separator arm admits exactly the spec separator's keys at the output and input tiers. `_localSeparatorIsSpecValid` says the value types of the keys the arm admits are ones the spec's separator accepts at both tiers. `extends` ignores extra keys, so the key agreement is carried by the first two: the third alone passes a labelled arm, and it is vacuous on BASE. "Admits" means a key whose type is not `never`. The two remaining blockers (`visible: boolean`, and `pinned` / `defaultOpen`) are unchanged, and so is the umbrella verdict.
- `@object-ui/types` zod mirror (fix round 1): `NavigationItemSchema`'s refinement has an explicit separator branch, and it used to return early, so `objectui validate` passed a separator `label` that the save door refuses with 422. That branch now refuses every key the spec's separator does not declare, each at its own path, with a message that names the key and the fix ("a separator carries only `type`, `id` and `order`; drop `label`"). The allowed set is read off the spec, not restated: the spec does not export `SeparatorNavItemSchema`, so it is taken from the separator arm of the spec `AppSchema`'s own `navigation` union. That schema already crosses the mirror's import boundary, so the objectui#8317 population is unchanged. The read throws if the arm is ever missing, instead of silently allowing everything.
- `@object-ui/plugin-designer`: `AppCreationWizard`'s "Add separator" and `NavigationDesigner`'s two add paths (now one `newNavItem` helper) write `{ id, type }`. `NavigationDesigner` no longer writes a `label` onto a new separator, and its label, icon and visibility patchers skip one.
- The union makes code that writes an entry-only key onto an unnarrowed item fail to compile, and each such site now narrows first. None of these edits changes what renders for valid data.
  - `@object-ui/layout`: `resolveNavItemLabel` answers `''` for every separator. A stored separator carrying a non-empty `label`, which `menuItemToNavigationItem` produced before this change, used to resolve to that label. No renderer asks it for a separator's label. The mobile bottom nav's leaf list, which already skipped separators, is typed as entries. `collectPinnedItems` tests the type before `pinned`.
  - `@object-ui/app-shell`: `useNavPins` registers a favorite only for an entry and leaves a separator as it is. The Studio sidebar's navigation walk passes a separator through unchanged.
  - Test fixtures that spread an item and add `visible` or `requiredPermissions` are typed as `NavigationEntryItem`. These are in layout's `AppSchemaRenderer` and `resolveHref` tests and app-shell's `UnifiedSidebar.derivedAreaVisibility` test.

**Member 2 — an edit keeps the stored branding.** `EditAppPage` now merges `branding` one level down, by the objectui#10842 rule. It keeps every stored key the spec's `AppBrandingSchema` declares, read from `AppBrandingSchema.shape`, and the wizard's values win for the keys it maintains. A stored `accentColor` survives the save. A stored key the spec does not declare is still left out.

**Member 3 — the Layout control is gone.** `AppWizardDraft.layout` is removed. The Basic Info step's Layout fieldset is removed, with its three icons and the draft default. `EditAppPage` no longer pre-fills `layout`. The step description now reads "Name, title, and icon". The four `appDesigner` layout keys are removed from `DESIGNER_DEFAULT_TRANSLATIONS` and from all ten locale packs, and `appDesigner.stepBasicDesc` is retranslated in all ten.

**Text that the change made false:**
- the `app.ts` module header and the `NavigationArea` docblock;
- the `wizardDraftToAppSchema` docblock;
- the `@object-ui/types:NavigationItem` and `@object-ui/types:NavigationItemSchema` ledger reasons in `scripts/check-spec-symbol-derivation.mjs` (the second now counts four divergences, not five);
- the mirror's own `NavigationAreaSchema` docblock, which listed a separator `label` among the keys only the spec refuses;
- the "separator label" row in `navigation-spec-parity.test.ts`: the faces now agree, so it left the divergence list and is asserted as an agreement (both refuse it);
- the ROADMAP line for the wizard's Basic Info step.

**Changesets.**
- New `.changeset/10867-app-wizard-saves-spec-app.md`: `@object-ui/types` and `@object-ui/i18n` minor (removing published pack keys is a narrowing), and `@object-ui/plugin-designer`, `@object-ui/layout` and `@object-ui/app-shell` patch, with the `Clause-②: yes` line. The BREAKING (authoring) banner names every consequence, and each was checked against the code at TypeScript 6.0.3 by a throwaway probe:
  - a read of `label` into a `string` slot fails (TS2322);
  - a spread of an entry-only key fails (TS2322);
  - `interface … extends NavigationItem` fails (TS2312);
  - an augmentation of `NavigationItem` fails (TS2300);
  - `objectui validate` refuses a separator `label`;
  - `t()` on a removed key renders the raw key unless the call passes a `defaultValue`. The provider-less fallback is the defaults table, then `defaultValue`, then the key, and i18next is configured with `returnNull: false` and no missing-key parser.
- Dated notes in the objectui#10533 form on two pending entries.
  - `10842-wizard-app-declared-keys.md`, titled "the wizard has no layout choice": its "the wizard's layout choice is not saved" has no choice left. Frontmatter md5 `5b8e68791c8bc51ef72179570fd15a1c` before and after.
  - `3162-types-ledger-batch8-verdicts.md`: its "three semantic blockers" count. Frontmatter md5 `2ee28f1e1b449ccc2dd97fdcc6c2bc1f` before and after.

**Fixture triage:**
- The `layout` key was dropped from the `AppWizardDraft` fixtures in `app-creation-types`, `app-declared-keys-10842` and `app-logo-one-spelling-10827`. These are spelling fixes: the key was there only because the type required it.
- The vacuous `'layout' in schema` assertion in `app-creation-types` "should handle draft with empty navigation" was removed.
- `navigation-model`'s "should convert a separator" pinned the removed `label: ''` branch, so it was replaced by an exact-shape assertion.
- The `label: ''` was dropped from separator fixtures in `navigation-model`, layout's `AppSchemaRenderer.test` and app-shell's `phase1-page-blocks.render.test`.

## H1 to H3 (measured on BASE `b93e245f9`, installed `@objectstack/spec` 17.4.0)

**H1 — reproduced.** A probe run through `wizardDraftToAppSchema`, then the spec's `AppSchema.safeParse`:
- a draft with one object entry plus the separator the wizard wrote, `{ id, type: 'separator', label: '' }`, gave `[{"code":"unrecognized_keys","path":"navigation.1","keys":["label"]}]`;
- control, the same draft without the separator: parses green;
- control, the same separator without `label`: parses green;
- `menuItemToNavigationItem({ type: 'separator', label: 'Section' })` gave `{"id":"migrated_0","type":"separator","label":"Section"}`.

The new DOM pin gives the same reading through the real wizard and `CreateAppPage` on the base source: "the saved document parses green through the spec `AppSchema`" fails with `unrecognized_keys` `["label"]` at `navigation.1`.

**H2 — reproduced.** The new pin "a stored `accentColor` survives the edit round trip" drives the real wizard through `EditAppPage`. On the base source it fails: the saved `branding` is `{ favicon, logo, primaryColor }`, and `"accentColor": "#f59e0b"` is missing.

**H3 — census** (`git grep` over packages, apps, docs, examples, skills and content). Each hit goes or is corrected:
- **`AppWizardDraft.layout` and the draft default:**
  - the member in `app.ts` — removed;
  - `DEFAULT_DRAFT.layout` in `AppCreationWizard` — removed;
  - `EditAppPage`'s `layout: appToEdit.layout || 'sidebar'` pre-fill — removed;
  - four draft fixtures — the key dropped (see the triage above).
- **The step's UI:** the Layout fieldset (`app-layout-*` test ids, `draft.layout` reads and writes) and its three icon imports — removed.
- **The step's strings:**
  - `appDesigner.layout`, `layoutSidebar`, `layoutHeader` and `layoutEmpty` in `DESIGNER_DEFAULT_TRANSLATIONS` and in ten locale packs — removed;
  - `appDesigner.stepBasicDesc` ("Name, title, and layout") in eleven places — corrected.
- **Docs:** the ROADMAP Basic Info line — corrected. `content/docs/guide/console.md` and `console-architecture.md` describe the wizard's four steps and never the Layout control, so they are unchanged.
- **Not this member:** the `layout: 'sidebar'` hits in `content/docs/core/app-schema.mdx`, `content/docs/guide/schema-overview.md`, the runner tests and the `AppComponentSchema` fixtures are `AppComponentSchema.layout`, the renderer node's own layout strategy. They are untouched, and the changeset says so.

## Pins and ablation

New pins:
- `packages/types/src/__tests__/app-wizard-separator-layout-10867.test.ts`: vitest halves, and `@ts-expect-error` / `satisfies` halves run under `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json`.
- `packages/plugin-designer/src/__tests__/AppWizard.specDocument-10867.test.tsx`: drives the real `AppCreationWizard` through `CreateAppPage` and `EditAppPage` and reads what reaches `saveItem`.
- The `spec-derived-unions.test.ts` agreement pins.
- Fix round 1: `packages/types/src/__tests__/nav-separator-mirror-refusal-10867.test.ts`. `safeValidateSchema`, the strict authoring face (`StrictAnyComponentSchema`) and the mirror itself each refuse a separator `label`, each at its own path; the mirror also refuses `icon` and `pinned` on a separator. Controls: a bare `{ id, type: 'separator' }` (and one with `order`) is accepted by both faces and the spec, the spec refuses the same `label`, and an entry keeps its `label`.
- Fix round 1: a new `EditAppPage` row, "a logo the author clears saves as cleared, not as the stored value". It is a guard, not a red-on-BASE pin: green on BASE and on HEAD, it fails if a later tidy-up drops empty strings from the merge.

**Red on BASE.** Run from a committed tree: the source files were checked out at BASE, the new pins kept, and everything was restored from `HEAD` under a trap. The restore was proven by blob hash equal to HEAD and an empty `git diff HEAD`.
- vitest `Tests 8 failed | 6 passed (14)`. The 8 failures are every non-control row:
  - `menuItemToNavigationItem`;
  - the two create-with-separator rows;
  - the three branding rows;
  - the two Layout rows.
- The 6 passes are the controls and compile-only rows.
- `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` in `packages/types` gives the new pins':
  - TS2741 ×2 (a bare separator is missing `label`);
  - TS2578 ×2 (unused `@ts-expect-error` for a labelled separator and for a draft with `layout`);
  - TS1360 ×3 (the no-`layout` `satisfies` and the two separator-agreement pins).

**Red before the mirror fix (round 1).** From the committed round-1 head, only `app.zod.ts` was checked out at the round-0 head `e2493c796`, under a trap; the restore was proven blob == HEAD and `git diff HEAD` empty. The new mirror pins plus `navigation-spec-parity` gave vitest `Tests 4 failed | 17 passed (21)`. The 4 failures are the refusal rows and the new agreement row; the controls passed.

**Green on HEAD.** Round 0, at `e2493c796`: `Test Files 284 passed (284)`, `Tests 5676 passed (5676)`. Round 1, at `2c19f3047`: see Gates. The `packages/types` `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` has 0 errors at both heads.

**Ablation: the separator branch is reverted, and only the separator rows redden.** Three anchored mutations went through `ablation-replace.mjs`, each proven landed and restored by blob hash:
- the `NavigationItem` alias gives its separator arm a required `label` again;
- `menuItemToNavigationItem` writes `label` again;
- the wizard's add-separator writes `label: ''` again.

Result:
- vitest `Tests 3 failed | 11 passed (14)`. The failures are `menuItemToNavigationItem`, "the saved document parses green" and "the saved separator carries only `type` and `id`". The branding and Layout rows stay green.
- `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json`: 5 errors, all on separator lines. TS2322 ×2 (bare separators), TS2578 ×1 (labelled separator) and TS1360 ×2 (the two agreement pins). The Layout type pin stays green.
- Restore: `blob == HEAD` and `git diff HEAD` empty for both files.

**Cross-package reverse check.** The downstream type-checks resolve `@object-ui/types` through its rebuilt `dist`. Their first runs went red only on sites the new union refuses: layout 3, plugin-designer 4, app-shell 3 in source plus 4 in tests. They were green after narrowing. That red could only come from the rebuilt declaration.

## Gates

